{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review Social Services and Child Protection Procedures for Section 20 powers",
        "additional_details": "We call for an urgent review to look at how to reform the child-protection system to prevent unnecessary separation, confusion and long-term harm to children and families. Parents must not be pressured or misled into agreeing to Section 20 accommodation. They must receive clear, accurate information, independent legal advice and a genuine explanation of their rights. We believe if they have demonstrated that no solicitor was present during the period they signed, then the application ought to be automatically denied.",
        "background": "We call for an urgent review into the use of section 20 powers. We are concerned that there is a lack of oversight, transparent decision-making, proper recording of consent, regular reviews and accessible complaints procedures. Parents must be told how to challenge decisions and raise concerns.",
